#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Picture"
msgstr "Imatge"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Picture</guilabel> tab displays a picture of the element when "
"available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bohr Orbitals"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Atom Model</guilabel> tab displays the atomic shells. Every "
"orbit stands for a atomic shell and every yellow circle represents an "
"electron."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "Chemical Data"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Chemical Data</guilabel> tab presents some atomic data. The "
"first entry is the <guilabel>Orbital structure</guilabel>. The next is the "
"<guilabel>density</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on the data available in &kalzium; you will see different radii of "
"the element. The covalent radius is the radius of a non charged atom of the "
"element in a molecule. The could for example be the O-H-distance in Water. "
"The atomic radius is the radius of an elemental atom, &eg; not bound to "
"anything. The van der Waals-radius is defined as the distance of two atoms "
"of the same sort in two equal molecules, for example two carbon-atoms in "
"propane. The last possible radius is the ionic radius including its charge."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The mass of an element is the avarage mass of all isotopes in relation to "
"their percentage."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some elements have information about their isotopes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mass"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid "The mass of this isotope."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "Neutrons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "The number of neutrons this isotope has."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "Percentage"
msgstr "Percentatge"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The percentage of atoms occuring that are of this isotope type. Also called "
"abundance."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "Half-life period"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Only unstable isotopes have a half-life period. It is defined as the time in "
"which half the isotopes decay."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid "Energy and Mode of Decay"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some isotopes are known to emit particle radiation under the process of "
"radioactive decay. Each decay transformation has a typical energy release, "
"which is listed along with the mode of decay."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spin and parity"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "The spin of the nucleus and its parity."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid "Magnetic Moment"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The magnetic dipolemoment of the nucleus. Measured in units of the nuclear "
"magneton."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Miscellaneous</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Miscellaneous</guilabel> tab tells you other informations "
"about the current element, including when it was discovered, its mean mass "
"(the mass per neutron) and the origin of the name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "Chemical Energies"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Energies</guilabel> tab tells you about different energy facts "
"related to the element."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spectrum"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "Numeration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The numeration is the way of numbering the 18 groups of the periodic table. "
"You can change the numeration to <guilabel>IUPAC</guilabel>, <guilabel>old "
"IUPAC</guilabel> or <guilabel>CAS</guilabel>, or you can switch it off "
"entirely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following options in the <guimenu>View</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Numeration</guimenuitem> menu can be used to change the "
"numeration shown:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>No Numeration</guimenuitem>: if this option is active, no "
"period-numeration will be in effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Show IUPAC</guimenuitem> (default): the <acronym>IUPAC</"
"acronym> is the <firstterm>International Union of Pure and Applied "
"Chemistry</firstterm>. This is an organization which defines most of the "
"standards for chemical concerns. The new IUPAC system numbers each column "
"with Arabic numbers from 1 (one) through 18 (eighteen)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Show CAS</guimenuitem>: the <acronym>CAS</acronym> is the "
"<firstterm>Chemical Abstracts Service</firstterm>. In the CAS system the "
"letters A and B were designated to main group elements (A) and transition "
"elements (B). Though the <acronym>IUPAC</acronym> numeration is the "
"official, the <acronym>CAS</acronym> numeration is what is still used in "
"classrooms and laboratories."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Show Old IUPAC</guimenuitem>: the old IUPAC system labeled "
"columns with Roman numerals followed by either the letter <quote>A</quote> "
"or <quote>B</quote>. Columns were numbered such that columns one through "
"seven were numbered <quote>IA</quote> through <quote>VIIA</quote>, columns 8 "
"through 10 were labeled <quote>VIIIA</quote>, columns 11 through 17 were "
"numbered <quote>IB</quote> through <quote>VIIB</quote> and column 18 was "
"numbered <quote>VIII</quote>. Because of the confusion the old IUPAC and the "
"CAS system created, the IUPAC adopted their new system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color schemes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalzium; can show you which elements are where with regard to their "
"Periodic <quote>block</quote> and <quote>group</quote>, their behavior with "
"acid and which state of matter (&ie; solid/liquid/vapor) they are in at a "
"given temperature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:419
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Color schemes can be changed in the <guimenu>View</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Look</guimenuitem> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>No Color Scheme</guimenuitem>: all the elements have the same "
"color. You can change the default color by choosing "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kalzium;...</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> and going to the <guilabel>Colors</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Show Groups</guimenuitem>: displays a color for each group. A "
"group is a vertical column in the periodic table of the elements. There are "
"18 groups in the standard periodic table. Elements in a group have similar "
"configurations of their valence shell electrons, which gives them similar "
"properties."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Show Blocks</guimenuitem>: displays a color for each block."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Show Acid Behavior</guimenuitem>: represents each acidic "
"behaviour with a different color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Show Family</guimenuitem>: represents each of the nine families "
"with a color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Show Crystal Structures</guimenuitem>: colors each element "
"depending on its crystal structure."
msgstr ""

